; bal -V --unrealized --dc keeps the report's debit and credit columns.
; Under --dc the running total is a pair of debit and credit amounts, so
; each posting's cost enters the baseline through the same amount
; expression.  A baseline of plain amounts, subtracted from that pair,
; would print the gross columns ($1700 and $1500) as the unrealized row
; and total both columns to zero.  One lot bought at $150 and valued at
; $170 prints a $200 revaluation in the debit column, and both columns
; total $1500, as before the balance report valued postings at cost.

2024/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Brokerage        10 AAPL @ $150
    Assets:Checking

P 2024/03/01 AAPL $170

test bal -V --unrealized --dc
         $1700          $1500           $200  Assets
         $1700              0          $1700    Brokerage
             0          $1500         $-1500    Checking
          $200              0          $-200  Equity:Unrealized Gains
-------------- -------------- --------------
         $1500          $1500              0
end test

test bal --exchange $ --unrealized --dc
         $1700          $1500           $200  Assets
         $1700              0          $1700    Brokerage
             0          $1500         $-1500    Checking
          $200              0          $-200  Equity:Unrealized Gains
-------------- -------------- --------------
         $1500          $1500              0
end test
